  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.066,
      0.723,
      0.082
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "This model in [35] is equivalent to our construction when the sign is flipped. Notice that",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.401,
      0.092,
      0.603,
      0.107
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nU _ {i} = Z _ {8 i + 1} Z _ {8 i + 3} Z _ {8 i + 5} Z _ {8 i + 7}\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.083,
      0.118,
      0.327,
      0.133
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "is a symmetric operator, we have",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.16,
      0.142,
      0.846,
      0.187
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\left(- \\sum_ {I} \\tilde {P} _ {I, I + 1}\\right) \\prod_ {i = 1} ^ {[ L / 8 ]} U _ {i} = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l l} \\prod_ {i = 1} ^ {[ L / 8 ]} U _ {i} \\left(- \\sum_ {I} P _ {I, I + 1}\\right) & L \\equiv 0 \\mod 8 \\\\ \\prod_ {i = 1} ^ {[ L / 8 ]} U _ {i} \\left(- \\sum_ {I} P _ {I, I + 1} - \\bar {P} _ {L / 4 - 1, L / 4} - \\bar {P} _ {L / 4, L / 4 + 1}\\right) & L \\equiv 4 \\mod 8 \\end{array} \\right.\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.195,
      0.134,
      0.208
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "where",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.291,
      0.216,
      0.715,
      0.245
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nP _ {I, I + 1} = \\frac {1}{4} (1 + Z _ {4 I - 3} X _ {4 I - 1} Z _ {4 I + 1}) (1 + Z _ {4 I - 1} X _ {4 I + 1} Z _ {4 I + 3}),\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.289,
      0.247,
      0.718,
      0.275
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\bar {P} _ {L / 4 - 1, L / 4} = \\frac {1}{4} (1 + Z _ {L - 7} X _ {L - 5} Z _ {L - 3}) (1 - Z _ {L - 5} X _ {L - 3} Z _ {L - 1}),\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.334,
      0.277,
      0.672,
      0.306
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\bar {P} _ {L / 4, 1} = \\frac {1}{4} (1 - Z _ {L - 3} X _ {L - 1} Z _ {1}) (1 + Z _ {L - 1} X _ {1} Z _ {3}).\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.083,
      0.313,
      0.919,
      0.344
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Thus the local projector is \\( P_{I,I + 1} \\) with exceptions on the boundary, which correspond to local symmetric defects. Since a phase is at the thermodynamic limit, the phase realized in [35] is equivalent to",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.435,
      0.353,
      0.569,
      0.385
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nH = - \\sum_ {I} P _ {I, I + 1}.\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.394,
      0.519,
      0.41
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "The component of \\(P_{I,I + 1}\\) in each sector can be expanded as",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.217,
      0.418,
      0.789,
      0.576
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\begin{array}{l} P _ {e} = \\frac {1}{4} \\begin{array}{c c c c c c} & e & e & s & s & r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} \\\\ \\hline & e & e & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ & s & s & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ & r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} & - 1 & - 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ & s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} , \\\\ P _ {s} = \\frac {1}{4} \\begin{array}{c c c c c} & e s & s e & s r ^ {2} r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} s r ^ {2} \\\\ \\hline e s & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ s e & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ s r ^ {2} r ^ {2} & - 1 & - 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ r ^ {2} s r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} , \\\\ P _ {r ^ {2}} = \\frac {1}{4} \\begin{array}{c c c c c} & e r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} e & s s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} s \\\\ \\hline e r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ r ^ {2} e & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ s s r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ s r ^ {2} s & - 1 & - 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} , \\\\ P _ {s r ^ {2}} = \\frac {1}{4} \\begin{array}{c c c c c} & e s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} e & s r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} s \\\\ \\hline e s r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ s r ^ {2} e & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ s r ^ {2} & 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\\\ r ^ {2} s & - 1 & - 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} \\\\ \\end{array}\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.583,
      0.135,
      0.597
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Define",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.269,
      0.603,
      0.735,
      0.637
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nm _ {e} = \\frac {\\left| \\begin{array}{c c c c c} e & e & s & s & r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} \\\\ \\hline e & 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} \\right|}{s} \\text {,} \\quad m _ {s} = \\frac {\\left| \\begin{array}{c c c c c} e & s & s & e & s r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} \\\\ \\hline 1 & 1 & - 1 & 1 \\end{array} \\right|}{s},\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.249,
      0.639,
      0.756,
      0.672
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nm _ {r ^ {2}} = \\frac {1}{r ^ {2}} \\left| \\begin{array}{c c c c} e r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} e & s s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} s \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\end{array} \\right., \\quad m _ {s r ^ {2}} = \\frac {1}{s r ^ {2}} \\left| \\begin{array}{c c c c} e s r ^ {2} & s r ^ {2} e & s r ^ {2} & r ^ {2} s \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & - 1 \\end{array} \\right..\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.68,
      0.127,
      0.694
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Then",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.456,
      0.702,
      0.548,
      0.731
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nP = \\frac {1}{4} m ^ {\\dagger} m.\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.739,
      0.414,
      0.755
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "We can then extract the cocycle gauge by \\( m \\):",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.26,
      0.762,
      0.744,
      0.781
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\n\\omega (r ^ {2}, r ^ {2}) = \\omega (s r ^ {2}, r ^ {2}) = \\omega (r ^ {2}, s) = \\omega (s r ^ {2}, s) = - 1, \\quad \\omega (\\mathrm{others}) = 1.\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.789,
      0.794,
      0.806
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "Thus the Hamiltonian of [35], for either \\( L = 0 \\mod 8 \\) or \\( L = 4 \\mod 8 \\), matches our model locally",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.405,
      0.814,
      0.598,
      0.851
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "\\[\nH = - \\frac {1}{4} \\sum_ {i} m _ {i, i + 1} ^ {\\dagger} m _ {i, i + 1}.\n\\]"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.084,
      0.859,
      0.517,
      0.874
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "And the MPO \\(A_{\\sigma}\\) acts on ground state as \\(\\mathrm{Tr}(A_{\\sigma})|e\\rangle = 2|e\\rangle\\).",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "bbox": [
      0.099,
      0.874,
      0.921,
      0.89
    ],
    "angle": 0,
    "content": "The third model is constructed similarly. After applying the CZ gate, the ground state is stabilized by the generator",
    "merge_prev": false
  },
  {
    "type": "equation",
    "bbox": [
      0.361,
